/-!
# Retracting an ind-étale algebra along a Jacobson-radical quotient

Let `A` be a w-contractible ring and `I ⊆ A` an ideal contained in the Jacobson radical of `A`,
equivalently an ideal whose zero locus meets the closure of every point of `Spec A`. Then the
lift of the trivial ind-étale `A ⧸ I`-algebra `A ⧸ I` across the quotient is `A` itself, and
consequently every `A`-algebra map `B → A ⧸ I` out of an ind-étale `A`-algebra `B` factors
through `A → A ⧸ I` by a unique `A`-algebra map `B → A`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.indEtaleQuotientLift_self_iso`: the lift of `A ⧸ I` is `A`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.existsUnique_algHom_comp_quotientMk_eq`: the unique compatible
  retraction, which is the ring-theoretic statement Stacks 09AC reduces to.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.indEtaleQuotientLift_isIso_unit_app_of_isWContractible` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.indEtaleQuotientLiftBaseChangeIso`: the relative form, at an
  arbitrary ind-étale algebra `C` with w-contractible ring in which `I · C` lies in the
  Jacobson radical — the lift of the quotient base change of `C` is `C`.

## Implementation notes

Write `L` for the lift of `A ⧸ I`. The counit of the lifting adjunction supplies an `A`-algebra
map `L → A ⧸ I`, so the image of `Spec L → Spec A` contains `V(I)`; since `I` lies in the
Jacobson radical, `V(I)` meets the closure of every point, and going down for the flat algebra
`L` makes that map surjective. Thus `L` is a faithfully flat ind-étale `A`-algebra and
w-contractibility of `A` produces a retraction `L → A`. That retraction is inverse to the
structure map `A → L` because the lift is fully faithful and `A ⧸ I` is initial among ind-étale
`A ⧸ I`-algebras, so `L` has exactly one endomorphism.

Correction to the argument of Stacks 09AC: the displayed identification `B ⧸ IB = A ⧸ I × R`,
and the ensuing replacement of `B` by a localization, are not used here, because they do not
follow — along a filtered colimit presenting an ind-étale algebra the idempotents generating the
kernel of a retraction only decrease, so that kernel need not be generated by one idempotent.
The lift `L` already satisfies `L ⧸ IL = A ⧸ I` by Stacks 097P, which is what the splitting was
for; and the uniqueness clause, omitted by the source, comes from full faithfulness of the lift
rather than from comparing local rings at maximal ideals.

The factorization statement is the resulting bijection between ring maps `B → A` splitting
`A → B` and ring maps `B → A ⧸ I` over `A`. It is obtained from the lifting adjunction composed
with the adjunction between pushout and restriction of scalars along `A → A ⧸ I`, so that no
pushout is ever computed: the bijection is evaluated using naturality of the two
hom-equivalences and the initiality of `A` in the under category of `A`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0981](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0981)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 097P](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/097P)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09AC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09AC)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale

/-! ### Faithful flatness along a Jacobson-radical quotient -/

/-- An ideal lies in the Jacobson radical exactly when it lies in every maximal ideal. -/
private theorem le_ringJacobson_iff_forall_isMaximal (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) :
    I ≤ Ring.jacobson A ↔ ∀ m : Ideal A, m.IsMaximal → I ≤ m := by
  rw [Ring.jacobson_eq_sInf_isMaximal, le_sInf_iff]
  exact Iff.rfl

/-- A flat `A`-algebra `B` carrying a ring map to `A ⧸ I` that extends the quotient map of `A`
is faithfully flat, provided `I` is contained in the Jacobson radical of `A`: a maximal ideal
`m` of `A` contains `I`, so the composite `B → A ⧸ I → A ⧸ m` contracts the zero ideal to a
prime of `B` lying over `m`. -/
private theorem faithfullyFlat_of_ringHom_quotient_of_le_ringJacobson
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (hI : I ≤ Ring.jacobson A)
    (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Module.Flat A B] (φ : B →+* A ⧸ I)
    (hφ : φ.comp (algebraMap A B) = Ideal.Quotient.mk I) :
    Module.FaithfullyFlat A B := by
  refine faithfullyFlat_of_forall_isMaximal_exists_comap_eq A B fun m hm ↦ ?_
  have him : I ≤ m := (le_ringJacobson_iff_forall_isMaximal A I).mp hI m hm
  have := hm
  let χ : B →+* A ⧸ m := (Ideal.Quotient.factor him).comp φ
  have hcomp : χ.comp (algebraMap A B) = Ideal.Quotient.mk m := by
    ext a
    simpa [χ] using congrArg (Ideal.Quotient.factor him) (RingHom.congr_fun hφ a)
  have : (⊥ : Ideal (A ⧸ m)).IsPrime := Ideal.isPrime_bot
  refine ⟨Ideal.comap χ ⊥, Ideal.IsPrime.comap χ, ?_⟩
  rw [Ideal.comap_comap, hcomp, ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, Ideal.mk_ker]

/-! ### The base ring as an ind-étale algebra over itself -/

/-- The quotient map of a ring by an ideal, as a morphism of commutative rings. -/
noncomputable abbrev quotientMkHom (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) :
    CommRingCat.of A ⟶ CommRingCat.of (A ⧸ I) :=
  CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)

/-- Morphisms of ind-étale algebras are exactly the morphisms of the underlying algebras. -/
def indEtaleAlgebraHomEquiv {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (X Y : IndEtaleAlgebra A) :
    (X ⟶ Y) ≃ (X.obj ⟶ Y.obj) where
  toFun f := f.hom
  invFun g := ObjectProperty.homMk g
  left_inv _ := rfl
  right_inv _ := rfl

/-- A ring regarded as an ind-étale algebra over itself through its identity map. -/
noncomputable abbrev indEtaleAlgebraSelf (A : Type u) [CommRing A] : IndEtaleAlgebra A :=
  ⟨Under.mk (𝟙 (CommRingCat.of A)),
    ObjectProperty.le_ind _ _ (RingHom.Etale.of_bijective Function.bijective_id)⟩

/-- A ring is the initial ind-étale algebra over itself. -/
noncomputable def indEtaleAlgebraSelfIsInitial (A : Type u) [CommRing A] :
    IsInitial (indEtaleAlgebraSelf A) :=
  IsInitial.ofUniqueHom (fun Y ↦ ObjectProperty.homMk (Under.mkIdInitial.to Y.obj))
    fun _ _ ↦ ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (Under.mkIdInitial.hom_ext _ _)

/-! ### The lift of the trivial algebra over a w-contractible ring -/

/-- A morphism of under objects commutes with the structure maps. -/
private theorem under_right_hom_apply {R : CommRingCat.{u}} {X Y : Under R} (f : X ⟶ Y) (a : R) :
    f.right.hom (X.hom.hom a) = Y.hom.hom a :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (Under.w f) a

/-- A ring map between the rings of two ind-étale `A`-algebras that is compatible with the
structure maps, as a morphism of ind-étale algebras. -/
private noncomputable def indEtaleAlgebraHomOfRingHom {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    (X Y : IndEtaleAlgebra A) (f : X.obj.right →+* Y.obj.right)
    (hf : ∀ a, f (X.obj.hom.hom a) = Y.obj.hom.hom a) : X ⟶ Y :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (Under.homMk (CommRingCat.ofHom f) (CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext hf)))

/-- **The lift of `A ⧸ I` is `A`.** For a w-contractible ring `A` and an ideal `I` contained in
the Jacobson radical of `A`, the lift of the trivial ind-étale `A ⧸ I`-algebra `A ⧸ I` across
the quotient `A → A ⧸ I` is `A` itself. -/
theorem indEtaleQuotientLift_self_iso (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (hA : ProetaleWContractible.IsWContractible.{u, u} A) (I : Ideal A)
    (hI : I ≤ Ring.jacobson A) :
    Nonempty (indEtaleAlgebraSelf A ≅
      (indEtaleQuotientLift A I).obj (indEtaleAlgebraSelf (A ⧸ I))) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨adj⟩ := indEtaleBaseChange_hasFullyFaithfulRightAdjoint A I
  obtain ⟨ff⟩ := indEtaleQuotientLift_fullyFaithful A I
  set V : IndEtaleAlgebra (A ⧸ I) := indEtaleAlgebraSelf (A ⧸ I)
  set L : IndEtaleAlgebra A := (indEtaleQuotientLift A I).obj V
  let _ : Algebra A L.obj.right := L.obj.hom.hom.toAlgebra
  have hmap : algebraMap A L.obj.right = L.obj.hom.hom := RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _
  -- `L` is ind-étale over `A`, hence flat.
  have hie : StacksDraft.IndEtale A L.obj.right := by
    refine indEtale_of_indEtaleUnder A L.obj.right ?_
    rw [hmap]
    exact L.property
  have hwe : Algebra.WeaklyEtale A L.obj.right := Algebra.weaklyEtale_of_ind_etale hie
  -- The counit, transposed along the pushout adjunction, is a ring map `L → A ⧸ I`
  -- extending the quotient map of `A`.
  let Q : L.obj ⟶ (Under.map (quotientMkHom A I)).obj V.obj :=
    (Under.mapPushoutAdj (quotientMkHom A I)).homEquiv L.obj V.obj (adj.counit.app V).hom
  have hQ : Q.right.hom.comp (algebraMap A L.obj.right) = Ideal.Quotient.mk I := by
    rw [hmap]
    exact RingHom.ext (under_right_hom_apply Q)
  -- Hence `L` is faithfully flat over `A`, and w-contractibility gives a retraction.
  have hff : Module.FaithfullyFlat A L.obj.right :=
    faithfullyFlat_of_ringHom_quotient_of_le_ringJacobson A I hI _ Q.right.hom hQ
  obtain ⟨ρ⟩ := indEtale_faithfullyFlat_retracts_of_isWContractible A hA L.obj.right hff hie
  -- The retraction and the structure map are mutually inverse.
  let r : L ⟶ indEtaleAlgebraSelf A :=
    indEtaleAlgebraHomOfRingHom _ _ ρ.toRingHom fun a ↦ by simpa [hmap] using ρ.commutes a
  have hsub : Subsingleton (L ⟶ L) :=
    @Equiv.subsingleton _ _ ff.homEquiv.symm
      ⟨fun f g ↦ (indEtaleAlgebraSelfIsInitial (A ⧸ I)).hom_ext f g⟩
  exact ⟨⟨(indEtaleAlgebraSelfIsInitial A).to L, r,
    (indEtaleAlgebraSelfIsInitial A).hom_ext _ _, hsub.allEq _ _⟩⟩

/-! ### Unique lifting of a section modulo a Jacobson-radical ideal -/

/-- Over a ring whose trivial ind-étale `A ⧸ I`-algebra lifts to `A`, the maps of ind-étale
`A`-algebras `X → A` correspond, by composing with `A → A ⧸ I`, to the ring maps `X → A ⧸ I`
over `A`. -/
private theorem exists_equiv_comp_quotientMk
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (j : indEtaleAlgebraSelf A ≅
      (indEtaleQuotientLift A I).obj (indEtaleAlgebraSelf (A ⧸ I)))
    (X : IndEtaleAlgebra A) :
    ∃ e : (X ⟶ indEtaleAlgebraSelf A) ≃
        (X.obj ⟶ (Under.map (quotientMkHom A I)).obj (indEtaleAlgebraSelf (A ⧸ I)).obj),
      ∀ f, (e f).right = f.hom.right ≫ quotientMkHom A I := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨adj⟩ := indEtaleBaseChange_hasFullyFaithfulRightAdjoint A I
  set V : IndEtaleAlgebra (A ⧸ I) := indEtaleAlgebraSelf (A ⧸ I)
  set L : IndEtaleAlgebra A := (indEtaleQuotientLift A I).obj V
  set Adj₀ := Under.mapPushoutAdj (quotientMkHom A I)
  let Q : L.obj ⟶ (Under.map (quotientMkHom A I)).obj V.obj :=
    Adj₀.homEquiv L.obj V.obj (adj.counit.app V).hom
  -- Composing with `j` is a bijection onto the maps into the lift.
  let e1 : (X ⟶ indEtaleAlgebraSelf A) ≃ (X ⟶ L) :=
    { toFun := fun f ↦ f ≫ j.hom
      invFun := fun g ↦ g ≫ j.inv
      left_inv := fun f ↦ by simp
      right_inv := fun g ↦ by simp }
  refine ⟨e1.trans ((adj.homEquiv X V).symm.trans
    ((indEtaleAlgebraHomEquiv _ V).trans (Adj₀.homEquiv X.obj V.obj))), fun f ↦ ?_⟩
  have hstep : Adj₀.homEquiv X.obj V.obj
      ((indEtaleQuotientBaseChange A I).map (f ≫ j.hom) ≫ adj.counit.app V).hom =
      (f ≫ j.hom).hom ≫ Q := by
    have hmap : (((indEtaleQuotientBaseChange A I).map (f ≫ j.hom) ≫
        adj.counit.app V).hom : (Under.pushout (quotientMkHom A I)).obj X.obj ⟶ V.obj) =
        (Under.pushout (quotientMkHom A I)).map (f ≫ j.hom).hom ≫ (adj.counit.app V).hom := rfl
    rw [hmap, Adj₀.homEquiv_naturality_left]
  have hinit : (j.hom.hom ≫ Q).right =
      ((Under.map (quotientMkHom A I)).obj V.obj).hom := by
    rw [Under.mkIdInitial.hom_ext (j.hom.hom ≫ Q) (Under.mkIdInitial.to _)]
    exact Under.mkIdInitial_to_right _
  show (Adj₀.homEquiv X.obj V.obj ((adj.homEquiv X V).symm (f ≫ j.hom)).hom).right = _
  rw [adj.homEquiv_counit, hstep]
  show (f.hom ≫ j.hom.hom ≫ Q).right = _
  rw [Under.comp_right, hinit]
  rfl

/-- **The ring-theoretic content of Stacks 09AC.** Let `A` be a w-contractible ring and `I ⊆ A`
an ideal contained in the Jacobson radical of `A`. Every `A`-algebra map from an ind-étale
`A`-algebra `B` to `A ⧸ I` factors through the quotient map `A → A ⧸ I` by a unique `A`-algebra
map `B → A`. -/
@[stacks 09AC "the ring-theoretic statement the lemma reduces to: for A w-contractible and \
I in the Jacobson radical, a factorization A -> B -> A/I with A -> B ind-etale has a unique \
retraction B -> A compatible with the maps to A/I; the source's B/IB = A/I x R splitting is \
not used, see the module docstring"]
theorem existsUnique_algHom_comp_quotientMk_eq (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (hA : ProetaleWContractible.IsWContractible.{u, u} A) (I : Ideal A)
    (hI : I ≤ Ring.jacobson A) (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (hB : StacksDraft.IndEtale A B) (φ : B →ₐ[A] A ⧸ I) :
    ∃! σ : B →ₐ[A] A, (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A I).comp σ = φ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨j⟩ := indEtaleQuotientLift_self_iso A hA I hI
  set X : IndEtaleAlgebra A :=
    ⟨Under.mk (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B)), indEtaleUnder_of_indEtale A B hB⟩
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_equiv_comp_quotientMk A I j X
  -- `φ`, read as a map of under objects.
  let v : X.obj ⟶ (Under.map (quotientMkHom A I)).obj (indEtaleAlgebraSelf (A ⧸ I)).obj :=
    Under.homMk (CommRingCat.ofHom φ.toRingHom) (CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext φ.commutes))
  -- A map of under objects into `A` is a retraction, and conversely.
  have hret : ∀ g : X ⟶ indEtaleAlgebraSelf A, ∀ a : A, g.hom.right.hom (algebraMap A B a) = a :=
    fun g ↦ under_right_hom_apply g.hom
  have hmk : ∀ g : X ⟶ indEtaleAlgebraSelf A, ∀ x : B,
      (e g).right.hom x = Ideal.Quotient.mk I (g.hom.right.hom x) := fun g x ↦
    RingHom.congr_fun (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (he g)) x
  refine ⟨{ toRingHom := (e.symm v).hom.right.hom, commutes' := hret (e.symm v) }, ?_, ?_⟩
  · refine AlgHom.ext fun x ↦ ?_
    have h := hmk (e.symm v) x
    rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply] at h
    exact h.symm
  · intro τ hτ
    refine AlgHom.ext fun x ↦ ?_
    let gτ : X ⟶ indEtaleAlgebraSelf A :=
      indEtaleAlgebraHomOfRingHom _ _ τ.toRingHom τ.commutes
    have hgτ : e gτ = v := by
      refine StructuredArrow.hom_ext _ _ (CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun y ↦ ?_))
      show (e gτ).right.hom y = φ y
      rw [hmk gτ y]
      exact AlgHom.congr_fun hτ y
    exact congrArg (fun g : X ⟶ indEtaleAlgebraSelf A ↦ g.hom.right.hom x)
      (e.eq_symm_apply.mpr hgτ)

/-! ### The lift of the quotient base change of a weakly contractible algebra -/

/-- A flat `R`-algebra `B` carrying an `R`-algebra map to `R ⧸ J`, for `J` inside the Jacobson
radical of `R`, is faithfully flat: every maximal ideal `m` of `R` contains `J`, so the
composite `B → R ⧸ J → R ⧸ m` exhibits a prime of `B` over `m`. -/
private theorem faithfullyFlat_of_algHom_quotient_of_le_ringJacobson
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (J : Ideal R) (hJ : J ≤ Ring.jacobson R)
    (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] [Module.Flat R B] (φ : B →ₐ[R] R ⧸ J) :
    Module.FaithfullyFlat R B :=
  faithfullyFlat_of_ringHom_quotient_of_le_ringJacobson R J hJ B φ.toRingHom
    (by ext a; simp)

/-- For a fully faithful right adjoint, the unit at an object is an isomorphism as soon as it
has a retraction. -/
private theorem isIso_unit_app_of_comp_eq_id {C D : Type*} [Category C] [Category D] {F : C ⥤ D}
    {G : D ⥤ C} (adj : F ⊣ G) (ff : G.FullyFaithful) {X : C} (ρ : G.obj (F.obj X) ⟶ X)
    (h : adj.unit.app X ≫ ρ = 𝟙 X) : IsIso (adj.unit.app X) := by
  have key : ∀ k : F.obj X ⟶ F.obj X, adj.unit.app X ≫ G.map k = adj.homEquiv X (F.obj X) k :=
    fun k => (adj.homEquiv_unit X (F.obj X) k).symm
  have h1 : adj.homEquiv X (F.obj X) (ff.preimage (ρ ≫ adj.unit.app X)) =
      adj.homEquiv X (F.obj X) (𝟙 (F.obj X)) := by
    rw [← key, ← key, ff.map_preimage, ← Category.assoc, h]
    simp
  refine ⟨ρ, h, ?_⟩
  rw [← ff.map_preimage (ρ ≫ adj.unit.app X), (adj.homEquiv X (F.obj X)).injective h1,
    CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
  rfl

/-- A morphism of ind-étale `A`-algebras is ind-étale. -/
private theorem indEtale_of_hom {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {C L : IndEtaleAlgebra A} (η : C ⟶ L) :
    letI := η.hom.right.hom.toAlgebra
    StacksDraft.IndEtale C.obj.right L.obj.right := by
  let _ : Algebra C.obj.right L.obj.right := η.hom.right.hom.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra A C.obj.right := C.obj.hom.hom.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra A L.obj.right := L.obj.hom.hom.toAlgebra
  have halgAC : (algebraMap A C.obj.right) = C.obj.hom.hom := RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _
  have halgAL : (algebraMap A L.obj.right) = L.obj.hom.hom := RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _
  have halgCL : (algebraMap C.obj.right L.obj.right) = η.hom.right.hom :=
    RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _
  have _ : IsScalarTower A C.obj.right L.obj.right := .of_algebraMap_eq fun a => by
    simp only [halgAL, halgAC, halgCL]
    exact (under_right_hom_apply η.hom a).symm
  exact StacksDraft.indEtale_of_comp
    (indEtale_of_indEtaleUnder A _ (by rw [halgAC]; exact C.property))
    (indEtale_of_indEtaleUnder A _ (by rw [halgAL]; exact L.property))

/-- The lift of the quotient base change of an ind-étale `A`-algebra `C` maps to `C ⧸ I · C`
compatibly with the unit and the quotient map. -/
private theorem exists_ringHom_quotient_comp_unit (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (adj : indEtaleQuotientBaseChange A I ⊣ indEtaleQuotientLift A I) (C : IndEtaleAlgebra A) :
    ∃ q : ((indEtaleQuotientLift A I).obj ((indEtaleQuotientBaseChange A I).obj C)).obj.right →+*
        C.obj.right ⧸ I.map C.obj.hom.hom,
      ∀ x, q ((adj.unit.app C).hom.right.hom x) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x := by
  let F := indEtaleQuotientBaseChange A I
  let G := indEtaleQuotientLift A I
  let b : CommRingCat.of A ⟶ CommRingCat.of (A ⧸ I) :=
    CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)
  let L : IndEtaleAlgebra A := G.obj (F.obj C)
  let η : C ⟶ L := adj.unit.app C
  let ε : F.obj L ⟶ F.obj C := adj.counit.app (F.obj C)
  have htri : F.map η ≫ ε = 𝟙 (F.obj C) := adj.left_triangle_components C
  have htri' : (F.map η).hom.right ≫ ε.hom.right = 𝟙 (F.obj C).obj.right := by
    conv_lhs =>
      rw [← Under.comp_right, ← ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, htri]
    simp
  let J : Ideal C.obj.right := I.map C.obj.hom.hom
  have hIJ : ∀ a ∈ I, (Ideal.Quotient.mk J).comp C.obj.hom.hom a = 0 := fun a ha =>
    Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)
  let kA : A ⧸ I →+* C.obj.right ⧸ J :=
    Ideal.Quotient.lift I ((Ideal.Quotient.mk J).comp C.obj.hom.hom) hIJ
  let w : (F.obj C).obj.right ⟶ CommRingCat.of (C.obj.right ⧸ J) :=
    pushout.desc (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)) (CommRingCat.ofHom kA) (by
      ext a
      exact (Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk I _ hIJ).symm)
  have hinl : pushout.inl C.obj.hom b ≫ w = CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) :=
    pushout.inl_desc _ _ _
  have hnat : η.hom.right ≫ pushout.inl L.obj.hom b =
      pushout.inl C.obj.hom b ≫ (F.map η).hom.right :=
    (pushout.inl_desc _ _ _).symm
  let q : L.obj.right ⟶ CommRingCat.of (C.obj.right ⧸ J) :=
    pushout.inl L.obj.hom b ≫ ε.hom.right ≫ w
  refine ⟨q.hom, fun x ↦ ?_⟩
  have e1 : (pushout.inl L.obj.hom b).hom (η.hom.right.hom x)
      = (F.map η).hom.right.hom ((pushout.inl C.obj.hom b).hom x) :=
    ConcreteCategory.congr_hom hnat x
  have e2 : ε.hom.right.hom ((F.map η).hom.right.hom ((pushout.inl C.obj.hom b).hom x))
      = (pushout.inl C.obj.hom b).hom x :=
    ConcreteCategory.congr_hom htri' ((pushout.inl C.obj.hom b).hom x)
  have e3 : w.hom ((pushout.inl C.obj.hom b).hom x) = Ideal.Quotient.mk J x :=
    ConcreteCategory.congr_hom hinl x
  show w.hom (ε.hom.right.hom ((pushout.inl L.obj.hom b).hom (η.hom.right.hom x))) = _
  rw [e1, e2, e3]

/-- **Stacks 09AC, affine case.** Let `C` be an ind-étale `A`-algebra whose ring is
w-contractible and in which the extended ideal `I · C` lies in the Jacobson radical. Then the
unit of the adjunction between quotient base change and its lift is an isomorphism at `C`. -/
public theorem indEtaleQuotientLift_isIso_unit_app_of_isWContractible
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (adj : indEtaleQuotientBaseChange A I ⊣ indEtaleQuotientLift A I)
    (C : IndEtaleAlgebra A)
    (hC : ProetaleWContractible.IsWContractible.{u, u} C.obj.right)
    (hjac : I.map C.obj.hom.hom ≤ Ring.jacobson C.obj.right) :
    IsIso (adj.unit.app C) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨ff⟩ := indEtaleQuotientLift_fullyFaithful A I
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := exists_ringHom_quotient_comp_unit A I adj C
  let L : IndEtaleAlgebra A :=
    (indEtaleQuotientLift A I).obj ((indEtaleQuotientBaseChange A I).obj C)
  let η : C ⟶ L := adj.unit.app C
  let _ : Algebra C.obj.right L.obj.right := η.hom.right.hom.toAlgebra
  have halgCL : (algebraMap C.obj.right L.obj.right) = η.hom.right.hom :=
    RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _
  have hwη := under_right_hom_apply η.hom
  have hCL : StacksDraft.IndEtale C.obj.right L.obj.right := indEtale_of_hom η
  have hwe : Algebra.WeaklyEtale C.obj.right L.obj.right :=
    Algebra.weaklyEtale_of_ind_etale hCL
  let φ : L.obj.right →ₐ[C.obj.right] C.obj.right ⧸ I.map C.obj.hom.hom :=
    { __ := q
      commutes' := fun x => by
        simp only [halgCL, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
        exact hq x }
  have hffCL : Module.FaithfullyFlat C.obj.right L.obj.right :=
    faithfullyFlat_of_algHom_quotient_of_le_ringJacobson C.obj.right _ hjac L.obj.right φ
  obtain ⟨σ⟩ := indEtale_faithfullyFlat_retracts_of_isWContractible C.obj.right hC
    L.obj.right hffCL hCL
  have hσ : ∀ x : C.obj.right, σ (η.hom.right.hom x) = x := fun x => by
    have hx := σ.commutes x
    rw [halgCL] at hx
    simpa using hx
  let ρ : L ⟶ C := indEtaleAlgebraHomOfRingHom _ _ σ.toRingHom fun a ↦ by
    rw [← hwη a]
    exact hσ _
  exact isIso_unit_app_of_comp_eq_id adj ff ρ (ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (by ext a; exact hσ a))

/-- **Stacks 09AC, affine case.** For an ind-étale `A`-algebra `C` with w-contractible ring in
which `I · C` lies in the Jacobson radical, the lift of the quotient base change of `C` is
isomorphic to `C`. -/
public theorem indEtaleQuotientLift_baseChange_iso_of_isWContractible
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (C : IndEtaleAlgebra A)
    (hC : ProetaleWContractible.IsWContractible.{u, u} C.obj.right)
    (hjac : I.map C.obj.hom.hom ≤ Ring.jacobson C.obj.right) :
    Nonempty ((indEtaleQuotientLift A I).obj ((indEtaleQuotientBaseChange A I).obj C) ≅ C) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨adj⟩ := indEtaleBaseChange_hasFullyFaithfulRightAdjoint A I
  have : IsIso (adj.unit.app C) :=
    indEtaleQuotientLift_isIso_unit_app_of_isWContractible A I adj C hC hjac
  exact ⟨(asIso (adj.unit.app C)).symm⟩

/-- The isomorphism `v(u(C)) ≅ C` of Stacks 09AC in the affine case, for an ind-étale
`A`-algebra `C` with w-contractible ring in which `I · C` lies in the Jacobson radical. -/
public noncomputable def indEtaleQuotientLiftBaseChangeIso
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (C : IndEtaleAlgebra A)
    (hC : ProetaleWContractible.IsWContractible.{u, u} C.obj.right)
    (hjac : I.map C.obj.hom.hom ≤ Ring.jacobson C.obj.right) :
    (indEtaleQuotientLift A I).obj ((indEtaleQuotientBaseChange A I).obj C) ≅ C :=
  Classical.choice (indEtaleQuotientLift_baseChange_iso_of_isWContractible A I C hC hjac)

